#### what this step proves: WHY two phase-A trials with identical poll timing end differently -- by sampling the proxy own switch list at 10 Hz across the window, so "the proxy still listed it" stops being an inference ####
# RE-RUN of step 10, which lost 4 of its 5 trials to a bug in THIS harness: wait_for_poll compared
# len(deque(maxlen=50)) against a snapshot, and once the deque filled it could never grow again.
# Fixed with a monotonic counter. The step-10 s7 trial is still valid and is carried forward.
# recipe: fire the power-off ~1.5 s before the next poll (phase A), then for 12 s record at 10 Hz
# whether /v1.0/topology/switches still lists the dpid. The kernel poll reaches the proxy at
# ~t_off+1.85 s and is applied at ~t_off+2.31 s (measured in 08_/09_).
